WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.562
Why does this rule exist?

2
00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:05.387
Because there are several ways to close
a finding without proving anything.

3
00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:07.685
The first is closure by ticket status:

4
00:00:07.685 --> 00:00:11.909
SailPoint's Service Desk integration
treats the mapped ServiceNow

5
00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:15.763
status as completion, and a person
can simply mark the work done.

6
00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:18.087
That's the example guide's first gap.

7
00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:23.314
The others are subtler: comparing against
an intended state that names nothing,

8
00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:26.957
which always matches; trusting
a read older than the fix;

9
00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:29.412
and treating a missing read as a match.

10
00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:31.440
This chapter closes all four.
